=== ISSUE #193: MCP tool handlers run on web-server task — no main-loop dispatch option ===
Labels: enhancement, needs-approach-review
Created: 2026-08-29T15:35:40Z

## Problem

`MCPToolRegistry` runs all tool handlers on the PsychicHttpServer web-server task. Any app module that implements `IMCPContributor` with **state-mutating** tools faces a threading hazard — the handler mutates app state from the wrong task.

This was discovered in the Wiser Controller app (DraytonWiserController PR-25 WO4, issue #37): five MCP command tools in `ThermostatController::registerMCPTools()` call semantic commands that mutate overlay arrays and effective-state snapshots that are **main-loop-confined** (no mutex by design — see the THREADING CONTRACT in `ThermostatController.hpp`).

### Current Wor
<truncated 4167 bytes>
t
// Boot sequence — fetch app branding FIRST
window.apiFetch("/api/app").then(function(data) {
  if (data.name) {
    document.getElementById("portal-title").textContent = data.name;
    document.title = data.name;
  }
  if (data.stylesheet) {
    var link = document.createElement("link");
    link.rel = "stylesheet";
    link.href = data.stylesheet;
    document.head.appendChild(link);
  }
  // THEN proceed with /api/tabs + script loading
  return window.apiFetch("/api/tabs");
}).then(function(tabs) {
  // ... existing boot sequence
});
```

This eliminates the title FOUC entirely and reduces the CSS FOUC to a single extra HTTP round-trip (which on localhost is <50ms).

#### Option B: Render-blocking CSS slot in index.html (zero FOUC)

Add a second `<link>` in the `<head>` that the build system can optionally populate:

```html
<head>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="app-brand.css" onerror="this.remove()">
</head>
```

If `/app-brand.css` exists → loaded render-blocking, zero FOUC.
If it 404s → the `onerror` handler removes the tag, no console error.

#### Option C: `Application::setAppStylesheet()` API

Add a `setAppStylesheet(const char* path)` method to `Application` (parallel to `setAppName()`). The `WebServerManager` includes it in the `/api/app` response and `app.js` injects it early.

### Workaround (current app-level hack)

Apps currently inject the CSS `<link>` from within a tab script IIFE:

```javascript
// Runs inside apikeys.js IIFE — too late, page already rendered
if (!document.getElementById("app-brand-css")) {
  var link = document.createElement("link");
  link.id = "app-brand-css";
  link.rel = "stylesheet";
  link.href = "/app-brand.css";
  document.head.appendChild(link);
}
```

This works but produces the visible FOUC described above.

### Environment

- Framework: PR #79 merge (cf869c7) — Portal Design System
- App: Departures Board v3
- Board: ESP32-S3-Nano

---END ISSUE---

